Sure! To change a `break` node’s label to `"loopEnd"` (but only if it isn’t already `"loopEnd"`), you’ll need to pass the node itself and the new label to the `updateBreak` function.

Here’s a quick example of how you’d call it:

```javascript
// Suppose this is your current break node (in string form)
const node = '{"type":"BreakStatement","label":"oldLabel"}';

// Call the function to update it
const result = updateBreak({
  node: node,
  label: "loopEnd"
});

console.log(result);
```

If the node’s label was already `"loopEnd"`, the function will simply return the original node unchanged. If you’re working directly with the AST object instead of a JSON string, just replace the `node` value with the actual object reference.
